style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>An issue with eSDK being host =
specific due to pseudo-native host dependencies has been resolved and =
this should resolve a number of bugs being reported by the community =
around use of the eSDK.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The prserv rewrite is still =
pending on resolving the issues with python =
asyncio.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We are continuing to make =
progress on the intermittent autobuilder failures. A race was identified =
in the qemu networking lock handling and there were some reproducibility =
fixes. Tweaks have been made to the autobuilder configuration such as =
avoiding key generation in more cases which it is believed may have been =
running into entropy shortages on the hosts, or just hitting CPU load =
issues. Some ptest improvements have also been =
made.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Despite this progress, we =
continue to see intermittent issues, particularly ptest ones. Help is =
very much welcome on these issues. You can see the list of failures =
we&#8217;re continuing to see by searching for the &#8220;AB-INT&#8221; =
tag in bugzilla: <a =
href=3D"https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?quicksearch=3DAB-IN=
T"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://bugzilla.yoctoproject.org/buglist.cgi?qui=
cksearch=3DAB-INT</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l10 =
level1 lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The multiconfig changes in =
bitbake continue to cause problems, we still need simpler test cases to =
reproduce issues rather than huge builds. The existing patches seem to =
fix some workloads and break others and current test cases are very slow =
to work with.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
